{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider asks the tribunal to 'review the whole fare', but the most this case can move is the arithmetic of POL-RD-02, and that arithmetic caps the refund well below the contested 12.87. On EV-FARE-00805 the charged total is 12.87; recomputed against the booked optimal of 2.5 km and 8.0 minutes, ((3.80 + 0.75 x 2.5 + 0.28 x 8.0) x surge 1.0) + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP and tolls + 0 fixed surcharges + 0 waiting time - 0 promo gives a recomputed fare of 8.715, a refund before rounding of 4.155, and a payable figure of 4.20. That is 32.3% of the charge, far below the 90% share that POL-RD-02 requires before a FULL_REFUND replaces the partial. The rider's exposure is therefore capped at 4.20 and the claim for the entire fare cannot succeed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00805", "EV-TRIP-00805"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.refund.payable",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The material deviation on this trip triggers the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check, and that check comes back negative on the clause's own test. driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d is 0 against driver_profile.completed_trips_90d of 300, so neither limb of the pattern test is satisfied: there is no count of 3 or more, and the ratio is 0.000 against the 0.05 threshold with well over 40 trips in the window. It follows that the rider cannot obtain the FULL_REFUND uplift under POL-RD-06(b), and no driver-conduct referral under POL-RD-06(c) is warranted. Under POL-GEN-01 no other profile field may be used for this test, including the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter, which is not the trailing-90-day figure the clause names.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00805"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "driver_profile.deviation_flags_90d",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No pass-through line enlarges the rider's position on this trip. EV-FARE-00805 carries no ERP gantry and no airport surcharge - erp_lines total is 0.00 and the trip ends at, rather than originates at, an airport, so the airport surcharge in the fare model is not chargeable and no POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity correction exists. A POL-RD-09 pass-through correction therefore adds nothing to the rider, and under POL-RD-09(1) no off-route ERP amount may be added on top of the POL-RD-02 figure. The total movement on this case stays at the single recomputed refund of 4.20 and nothing more.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00805", "EV-GPS-00805"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09", "POL-RD-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.components.fixed_surcharges",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own message is on the record and it is the reason this route is not a driver's invention: sent at 13:59:40 by the rider and read 20 seconds before the vehicle moved off, it asks the driver to 'stop at Golden Mile Tower first' and carries a waypoint hint. That satisfies POL-RD-04(a), (b) and (c) - it is the rider's instruction, it predates departure, and it names a place specifically. The corroboration limb, however, cannot be met on this trace, and the driver does not ask the tribunal to pretend otherwise: the nearest fix to the requested waypoint is 1,592.1 m, far outside the 200 m threshold POL-RD-04 sets, so no distance is excluded and no amended optimal is supplied. POL-RD-14 is explicit that this is a failed corroboration, not the mutually contradictory evidence described in POL-RD-10(7); the driver's reliance on the request is an explanation that the trace does not carry, not evidence of comparable strength against the trace.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00805", "EV-GPS-00805"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-RD-14"],
      "relies_on": "derived.waypoint_approach.messages[0].nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "This case is fully decidable on the bundle and does not meet any escalation trigger, so the disputed amount should be resolved by a monetary ruling rather than held. The trip identifier matches across EV-TRIP-00805, EV-GPS-00805 and EV-FARE-00805 and the timestamps are consistent; the trace is not impaired for policy purposes because none of POL-RD-07(a) to (c) fires - coverage is 100%, there are 90 fixes at a 10-second cadence, no gaps, and a maximum gap of 10 seconds, far under the 90-second limb. No charge line lacks a counterpart in the trace or trip record. The bundle holds no traffic advisory: EV-ADVIS-00805-01 is MISSING, carries issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT and has a weight_multiplier of 0.0, so its absence is citable but it can carry no fact - and because the driver asserts no external traffic cause and cites no advisory identifier, nothing is invoked against a missing artifact and POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged, while POL-RD-14 confines POL-RD-10(7) to the partly-corroborated case this is not.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00805", "EV-TRIP-00805", "EV-ADVIS-00805-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10", "POL-RD-14", "POL-RD-07"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 4.20,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "Both parties: the platform's own trace of trip TRP-00805 (EV-GPS-00805) measures 5.5 km driven between the recorded pickup and dropoff against a booked optimal of 2.5 km on EV-TRIP-00805 — an excess of 3.0 km, which is 120% of optimal. That clears both POL-RD-01 establishment tests (greater than 20% of optimal and greater than 0.8 km absolute) and is additionally a MATERIAL deviation on the percentage limb. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07(a)–(c): 90 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps, longest gap 10 seconds. No independent corroboration is therefore needed, and POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged. POL-RD-08 is satisfied: the trip id and timestamps are consistent across EV-TRIP-00805, EV-GPS-00805 and EV-FARE-00805, and the burden shifted to the driver.\n\nDriver: your explanation that you were following the rider's chat request to stop at Golden Mile Tower first (EV-CHAT-00805, MSG-00805-001, sent 13:59:40) does not excuse the excess. The instruction meets POL-RD-04(a)–(c), but POL-RD-04 also requires the trace to show the vehicle passing within 200 m of the requested waypoint, and the nearest fix is 1592.1 m away. Under POL-RD-14 the instruction did not cause the measured excess: no distance is excluded, and the deviation stands on the trace as measured. This is a failed corroboration, not the mutually contradictory evidence described in POL-RD-10(7). No traffic ground was asserted or cited; EV-ADVIS-00805-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT) and its absence is noted, but it carries no fact, so POL-RD-03 cannot be run and POL-RD-10(5) is not engaged (POL-RD-13).\n\nRemedy: the fare on EV-FARE-00805 is METERED with quoted_fare_sgd null, so POL-RD-11 does not run and POL-RD-02 governs. Charged total is 12.87. Recomputed fare = (3.80 base + 0.75 x 2.5 optimal km + 0.28 x 8.0 optimal min) x 1.0 surge multiplier read from EV-FARE-00805 + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP/tolls + 0 waiting time fee - 0 promo discount = 8.715. Refund = 12.87 - 8.715 = 4.155 before rounding, payable rounded UP to SGD 4.20. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and is 32.3% of the charge, far below the 90% share that would make it a FULL_REFUND. The ruling is therefore PARTIAL_REFUND of SGD 4.20 to the rider.\n\nDriver profile: the material deviation triggers the POL-RD-06 check, but deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 300 completed trips in 90 days, so no pattern is established — no FULL_REFUND uplift under POL-RD-06(b) and no driver-conduct referral under POL-RD-06(c). The lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter is context-only under POL-GEN-01 and was not used. Pass-throughs: EV-FARE-00805 carries no ERP gantry and no airport surcharge, so there is no POL-RD-09 correction and nothing is added on top of the POL-RD-02 figure, exactly as POL-RD-09(1) requires. No escalation trigger fires: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, identifiers and timestamps agree, the trace is unimpaired, no missing artifact was invoked as an exculpatory ground, and the refund is within the POL-RD-10(6) limits. The monetary effect of SGD 4.20 is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold on the policy given, so it executes automatically on issue."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

