    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "This is a route-deviation case about trip TRP-00805, and both parties largely agree on the facts. The platform's booking estimate was 2.5 km over 8.0 minutes (EV-TRIP-00805), and the trace measures 5.5 km actually driven (EV-GPS-00805). The excess is 3.0 km, which is 120% of the optimal distance and also 3.0 km in absolute terms, so both tests in POL-RD-01 are met and the deviation is established; at 120% it is additionally MATERIAL because that exceeds the 50% threshold. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes: 90 fixes at a 10-second cadence, 100% coverage, no gaps and a maximum gap of 10 seconds, none of which reaches POL-RD-07(a) to (c). No independent corroboration is therefore required and the POL-RD-10(3) escalation does not engage.\n\nTo the driver: you say you followed the rider's in-app request to stop at Golden Mile Tower first. That request is on the record (EV-CHAT-00805, MSG-00805-001, sent 13:59:40, before the vehicle moved, naming a specific place, with a waypoint hint), and it satisfies POL-RD-04(a) to (c). But POL-RD-04 also requires the trace to corroborate the instruction by passing within 200 m of the waypoint, and the platform's own waypoint match puts the nearest fix 1,592 m away (EV-GPS-00805). Under POL-RD-14 the instruction therefore did not cause the measured excess: no distance is excluded and the deviation stands at the measured figure. Your reliance on the request is an explanation the trace does not support, not evidence of comparable strength against it, so POL-RD-10(7) is not engaged. You also assert no external traffic cause, and the bundle holds no traffic advisory (EV-ADVIS-00805-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0), so no closure exoneration arises.\n\nTo the rider: the refund is the arithmetic of POL-RD-02, not the whole fare. Recomputed fare = ((3.80 + 0.75 x 2.5 optimal km + 0.28 x 8.0 optimal min) x 1.0 surge multiplier read from EV-FARE-00805) + 0.80 platform fee + 0 ERP and tolls + 0 fixed surcharges + 0 waiting time fee - 0 promo = 8.715. Charged total is 12.87, so the refund is 12.87 - 8.715 = 4.155, rounded up to SGD 4.20. That is above the SGD 0.50 de minimis floor and well below the 90% share that would make it a full refund, so the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND.\n\nNo pass-through line enlarges the position either way: EV-FARE-00805 charges no ERP and no airport surcharge, so POL-RD-09 adds nothing and nothing may be double-counted. The fare is METERED with no quoted fare, so POL-RD-11 does not apply. The POL-RD-06 driver-profile check comes back negative on its own test (deviation_flags_90d 0 against completed_trips_90d 300, ratio 0.000), so there is no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral; the lifetime prior_deviation_flags counter is not the field that clause names and was not used. Confidence: every artifact carrying a deciding fact (EV-GPS-00805, EV-TRIP-00805, EV-FARE-00805) sits at weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0, above the 0.70 floor. The refund is below the POL-GEN-05 execution threshold and issues automatically."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
